# TEST RANGE (MAPS' testrange_v1, John 17 Nov 19:35: "a range with buildings to blow up, with explosive objects in some.
# make it look simple but cover my needs"). For John's own testing, New Battle only: no mission script sends it.
# 60 x 40 x 3, .MAP2. Joes on the concrete firing pad behind the sandbags (south); six targets along the north edge:
#   A empty block hut, B hut with oil drums, C two-storey block house (stairs on the north side; propane downstairs,
#   ammo crates upstairs), D tin shed with generator, fuel pump and drums, E bunker with ammo crates, F fuel depot.
# Cars on the road row and loose drums, propane, ammo, a transformer, a generator and a fuel pump in the open.
#  Terrain order matters.
terrains:
  - name: TESTRANGE
    mapDataSets:
      - BLANKS
      - OUTYARD
      - OUTBASE
      - STATION
      - JCARS
    mapBlocks:
      - name: TESTRANGE
        width: 60
        length: 40
        height: 3
        groups: [0]
mapScripts:
  - type: TESTRANGE_SCRIPT
    commands:
      - type: addBlock
        size: [6, 4]
        groups: [0]
        rects:
          - [0, 0, 6, 4]
# The mission itself is BUILD-2's TEST RANGE (zz_gijoe_testbed.rul, STR_GJ_TESTBED): every Joe and vehicle against one of
# every Cobra unit, on this map. One mission, not two.
extraStrings:
  - type: en-US
    strings: &trStrings
      STR_TEST_RANGE: "Test Range"
      STR_TEST_RANGE_BRIEFING: "John's range. Six targets along the north edge, west to east: an empty block hut, a hut full of oil drums, a two-storey block house (propane downstairs, ammo upstairs, stairs on the north side), a tin shed, an ammo bunker and a fuel depot. Cars on the road and loose drums, propane, ammo, a transformer, a generator and a fuel pump in the open. One unarmed dummy in each target. Blow it all up."
  - type: en-GB
    strings: *trStrings
